rt0|a|Finished; brought to perfection; refined; hence, free from impurity; excellent; superior; elegant; worthy of admiration; accomplished; beautiful. ; Aiming at show or effect; loaded with ornament; overdressed or overdecorated; showy. ; Nice; delicate; subtle; exquisite; artful; skillful; dexterous. ; Not coarse, gross, or heavy ; Not gross; subtile; thin; tenous. ; Not coarse; comminuted; in small particles; as, fine sand or flour. ; Not thick or heavy; slender; filmy; as, a fine thread. ; Thin; attenuate; keen; as, a fine edge. ; Made of fine materials; light; delicate; as, fine linen or silk. ; Having (such) a proportion of pure metal in its composition; as, coins nine tenths fine. ; (Used ironically.) ; To make fine; to refine; to purify, to clarify; as, to fine gold. ; To make finer, or less coarse, as in bulk, texture, etc.; as. to fine the soil. ; To change by fine gradations; as (Naut.), to fine down a ship's lines, to diminish her lines gradually.	j:249w,55,4;nsy,54,6;1gnu,42,8;1rwa,40,11;vwu,34,13;1a5w,32,5;dxt,31,4;249l,25,24;vk7,24,9;k8e,23,1;1c3y,21,7;22bf,19,5;fm7,16,7;1kq9,16,6;1nh,15,6~249l,25,24;vwu,34,13;4pp,1,13;1rwa,40,11;2490,13,10;1p3q,8,10;22pi,6,9;vk7,24,9;1gnu,42,8;fm7,16,7;1rvm,10,7;1c3y,21,7;23f8,8,6;1nh,15,6;nsy,54,6	e:1hl5,8,128;pk4,4,4;19k7,3,1~1hl5,8,128;pk4,4,4;19k7,3,1
